From 16a6e69332bb4e5ea9918a25916c5645a5e5487e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:59:51 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(motion): adaptive growth overload fallback compares whole
 revolutions

Where no growth step holds the load, the step search kept the least
overload from readings cut short at the first point past the bound.
Where the overload does not grow with the step, every try read the same,
the largest step won the tie and was walked whole far past the reading
it was chosen on (island NE corner, #7 round 10: 59.5 deg chosen,
125 deg cut).

The tried revolutions are now walked whole again from the planner's
stock (least_whole), largest first; a smaller step replaces the kept one
only when it reads more than 2 % less, and each re-walk is abandoned once
it can no longer win. The re-walks rebuild no geometry and re-read only
revolutions whose whole length the trial already charged, so the #13
growth budget (WORK_MAX, GEOM_MAX/GEOM_LEN) is unchanged
(docs/decisions/845-adaptive-overload-fallback.md).

Pinned by grow::tests::the_overload_fallback_keeps_the_least_whole_reading_not_a_truncated_tie.

Fixes #845

